# ── Live data — NEVER commit these ───────────────────────────────────────────
# The bot writes to restocker.db constantly. Committing it means every push carries
# a stale snapshot, and every server pull fights (or overwrites) the live database.
# It stays on disk; it just must not travel through git.
restocker.db
restocker.db-journal
restocker.db-wal
restocker.db-shm
*.db
*.db-journal
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# Automatic DB backups (see db_backup_loop) — local to each machine.
backups/

# ── Runtime state the bot writes ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# The DB is the source of truth; these are its write-only mirrors and would cause
# the same pull conflicts if tracked. Some of them also hold PLAYER DATA — real
# Discord ids next to coin balances — and a rule here does nothing about a file
# git is already tracking. `data/state/balances.yml` and `data/state/web_user_prefs.yml`
# have been in this repo since before these rules existed; untracking them takes
# `git rm --cached`, and clearing them out of the history takes filter-repo.
data/state/*
data/csn_history/
data/exports/
# Restore snapshots: a point-in-time copy of market state, written by hand during
# an incident. Local to whoever made it.
data/restore_*/

# EXCEPTIONS — hand-maintained CONFIG the bot only READS. These must travel to the
# server through git like code does, so they are excepted from `data/state/*` above.
!data/state/brew_effects_manual.yml
!data/state/brew_aliases.yml
!data/state/market_tickers.yml

# Secrets / environment
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd
.venv/
venv/

# Editor / OS junk
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# working files (Claude)
*.xlsx
deploy.bat
deploy_log.txt
.fuse_hidden*

# ── Scratch, backups and tooling leftovers ───────────────────────────────────
# lock files moved aside by tooling — never belongs in git.
# Git creates .git/index.lock and removes it a moment later; a bridge that cannot
# delete leaves it behind, and GitHub Desktop then refuses to commit. They get
# moved here instead.
_git_stale_locks/
restocker.log
*.log
# scratch/backup copies — kept on disk, never pushed to the server
_to_delete/
_baseline/
_pre_audit_backup_*/
# transfer scratch dirs — never belong in git
_xfer*/

# Cowork transfer scratch
_incoming/
Restocker_web.py.bak.*
*.bak
*.bak.*

# Bundles and archives. `vtech_bundle.zip` is 21MB of working tree and arrived
# truncated once already; nothing in this repo should be a zip.
*.zip

# ── Things that were tracked before these rules existed ──────────────────────
# Each of these needs `git rm --cached` as well; a rule here only stops them
# coming BACK. See the untrack list in the handoff.
#
# The Windows tunnel binary. 52MB, and the code never runs it: `_start_cloudflared`
# execs `./cloudflared` — the Linux binary — so the .exe is local-dev weight only
# and the server downloads its own.
cloudflared.exe
cloudflared
# Dead mockups, superseded by abex_screens.py.
dashboard_redesign_*.html
# A one-off Windows helper that has already served its purpose.
untrack_db.bat
# Reports and workbooks: outputs, not source. `earnings_extended.xlsx` appears in
# Restocker_main only as a provenance STRING ("restore:earnings_extended.xlsx"),
# never opened, so untracking it changes no behaviour.
*.docx
csn_stock_MERGED.csv


# ── AbexTech monorepo ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Three bots, three tokens, three guilds, one checkout. Each keeps its own env
# file next to its own entry point; none of them travel through git.
bank/.env
stakes/.env
stakes/channels.json
bank/bank.db

# leftover from the old Restocker repo; nothing to do in a fresh history
_untrack.bat

# ── One-off scripts and stale handoff notes ──────────────────────────────────
# Untracked deliberately, not deleted: they still sit in the working folder as
# history. They were shipping to the server on every pull, and none of them is
# imported or executed by anything that runs there.
#
# NOT listed here, because they ARE imported and removing them breaks the boot:
#   seed_items.py       (run_core.py, main.py)
#   clean_item_names.py, migrate_market_id.py, ledger_migrate.py (Restocker_main.py)
#   healthcheck.py      (pre-deploy preflight -- useful ON the server)
apply_market_registry.py
fix_catalog_stacks.py
fix_hive_duplicates.py
fix_share_gifts.py
mint_code.py
AMAZONIA_ONBOARDING.md
AUDIT_*.md
DEPLOY_TEST.md
HANDOFF*.md
ONBOARDING_*.md
SW_Trade_Network_Integration.md
_PUSH_README.md
